date: 2026-06-06T22:12:21-04:00
---

The Sin and Tonic is a bar in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]]. Owned by [[Illmari Vaino]], it's the current headquarters of [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]].

The interior is dingy and dark, and Illmari keeps incense censors burning tobacco hanging from the ceiling during operating ours. The main serving area is a large rectangular room with booths along the walls and a bar in the center. The left exit leads to the workshop and garage, the right exit leads to the stockroom and armory, and the back exit leads to bedrooms and an office.

Unlike many a Fane — its walls sustained by a [[Hearts|Heart]] rather than mere brickwork — the [[Sin and Tonic]] makes no pretence of grandeur: the sleeping quarters are tucked at the back on the same level as the bar, the beds hovering somewhere around two-star comfort on a generous night. The the [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|twins]] are the greater draw for those in need, skilled enough to brew healing potions, though they run nothing so formal as a shop — bring your own components, or don't bother asking. A supermarket a few blocks off covers the more mundane resupply.

A radar dish taken from the roof of a roller rink is kept in the garage. The twins examined it and traced it to [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]], with its signal originating from a [[Org/Gryphonline/index|Gryphonline]] distribution center. A small arcane device that came with it, the [[Sentience Distributor]], spreads whatever signal the dish receives; it is fragile, and the the [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|twins]] advise against switching it on indoors.

The group's company car is called the day tripper, and members can sign it out of the garage in the alley. The day tripper was left behind at the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|Crowded Flea]] when the Party fled the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]], and the gang took it.

By the time the Party moved on [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]], the day tripper was in a bay of a [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]] auto body shop on Anchor Boulevard in Widdershins, where the gang had it on a hoist. The Party found its keys on a rack by the counter inside.

After the Party reported the fane beneath the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]] to the [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/index|Inquisition]], a pair of Inquisitors came to the bar, asked about its licensing in that part of town, saw the papers, and took the radar dish out of the garage as part of their investigation. The bar's staff take its messages, and a fax from [[Org/The Undertable/People/Smiler|Smiler]] reached the Party here.

The Party paid [[Org/The Undertable/People/Smiler|Smiler]] to register the black Aventine they took from the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] legally under [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]], and it became their car. [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Anouk]] asked them here to search for her missing brother.

The Party came back from [[People/Sbrtlby Jotes|Sbrtlby Jotes]]'s drug works with the [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Marchal]] twins and read over what they had taken from the demon at a booth; the paintings they had carried out of [[People/Valerius Vane|Vane]]'s manor were still in the armory with [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Elias Ramsey|Elias]], untouched. Before they set out again for the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus|Sub Transit Nexus]] the twins set them up with a portable radio tuned to the frequency they had asked for.
